# Inventory Page Consistency

- When changing a MES inventory, residual, or LOT calculation page, apply the rule to every product, color, LOT, and entry path on that page. Do not hard-code a fix for one displayed item.
- Before completing, verify that page summaries, LOT detail rows, history, selection dialogs, and save/validation paths use the same calculation source and unit.
- Preserve traceability: a manual adjustment without an identified LOT must be visibly labeled as LOT-unassigned; do not silently assign it to a real LOT.
- For every page, treat `AuthModule.canWritePage(pageId)` as the authority for normal registration and modification. Do not require an administrator merely because a user is editing data; reserve administrator checks for deletion, bulk reset, permission management, and other destructive operations.
